/docs/

# The generated API reference IS committed, deliberately.
#
# It used to be produced during the Pages deploy, which needed a cross-repo PAT
# to dispatch docfx in stellayazilim/Ergosfare and pull the metadata back. That
# secret was never configured, so the generation step silently skipped on every
# deploy and the whole /api section 404'd in production while working fine
# locally — a failure mode with no error anywhere.
#
# Committing the output removes the secret, the dispatch and the failure mode:
# the deploy just builds what is in the tree. The cost is ~340 machine-written
# files (~2.5 MB) to regenerate whenever the public API surface changes:
#
#   task api        # from the superproject — refreshes both documented lines
#
# Only docfx's intermediate metadata stays out; it is rebuilt from the .NET
# sources and nothing reads it after the conversion.
.api-cache/